## Durable development contract

Follow global `worker-dev` / `e2e-cockpit`: FIFO/tick only. Dispatch sequence 0
has no heartbeat; run the exact `accept-dispatch`, start only on `accepted` /
`start_work=true` (sequence 1), then `heartbeat` running sequence 2. Duplicates
never restart implementation. `ask` / `access-prompt` use private typed body
refs; `pending` / `read-question` return durable mission-status JSON. Only
explicit human replies; `hold --answers` leaves the prompt unapproved.
Inspect `status.pending_commands` and `command-status`; accepted-worker
cancel/replace needs accepted then applied ACK with matching digest and typed
`--result` after actual safe application. Reuse IDs/digests; journal no secrets.
Lifecycle is separate from pane diagnosis. No raw `send`/`nudge` for normal
mission, approval or cancel; uninstrumented prompts need explicit reporting.

If the parent repo has `graphify-out/graph.json` and `graphify` is available,
use `graphify query "<question>" --graph "$REPO/graphify-out/graph.json"`
before broad text search for related code, architecture, file relationships, and
implementation patterns.

